To isolate the background without affecting your face or clothing in apps like Lightroom, you can use the "Adjustment Brush" or "Gradient Filter" tools to selectively apply edits to the background. These tools allow you to paint or draw over specific areas of the image, applying adjustments such as blur or desaturation only to those areas. Alternatively, you can use the "Select and Mask" tool to manually select the background and apply edits to it, while protecting your face and clothing from the edits.

Regarding the photo's resolution, it's true that a higher resolution image will generally allow for more effective edits, especially when it comes to subtle adjustments like background blur or desaturation. However, LinkedIn's image compression algorithms may reduce the visible impact of these edits, especially if the image is highly compressed. To minimize the impact of compression, it's a good idea to save your edited image in a high-quality format (such as TIFF or PNG) and then upload it to LinkedIn. Additionally, be mindful of the image's aspect ratio and ensure that it is optimized for LinkedIn's display dimensions to avoid any unnecessary resizing or cropping.

